            <p>Pitanguy Line. This image illustrates the Pitanguy line, which runs from a point 5 mm inferior to the tragus to a point 15 mm superior to the lateral brow. This line approximates the course of the frontal branch of the facial nerve. Contributed by MH Hohman, MD, FACS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="PitanguyLine" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
